00:27:47.699 --> 00:27:50.274
Either that or Tommy
raising a fist to Jimmy,

526
00:27:50.309 --> 00:27:53.182
which is never a good idea.

527
00:27:53.250 --> 00:27:54.927
Where'd they bury him?

528
00:27:55.019 --> 00:27:57.516
In Jim's favorite spot.

529
00:27:57.586 --> 00:28:00.489
Right there under the
bridge in Neponset River.

530
00:28:01.905 --> 00:28:04.058
He buried so many bodies in that shithole,

531
00:28:04.140 --> 00:28:08.773
it became known as the
Bulger Burial Ground.

532
00:28:10.606 --> 00:28:13.075
I don't know how you fuckers didn't get it.

533
00:28:13.229 --> 00:28:15.860
I really don't. I mean, in the beginning,

534
00:28:15.979 --> 00:28:17.376
Jim was a small-town player

535
00:28:17.417 --> 00:28:20.203
who really only mattered in Southie.

536
00:28:20.377 --> 00:28:22.619
Don't get me wrong... he
was a tough motherfucker,

537
00:28:22.654 --> 00:28:25.510
but small-time.

538
00:28:25.760 --> 00:28:28.692
And then the next thing you
know, he's a goddamn kingpin.

539
00:28:29.035 --> 00:28:30.627
You know why?

540
00:28:31.420 --> 00:28:33.467
Because the FBI let it happen.

541
00:28:42.859 --> 00:28:44.246
This is John.

542
00:28:44.296 --> 00:28:46.265
Connolly.

543
00:28:47.278 --> 00:28:48.412
Jimmy.

544
00:28:48.445 --> 00:28:51.072
This is potentially
the biggest opportunity

545
00:28:51.107 --> 00:28:52.609
the Bureau will ever have had

546
00:28:52.681 --> 00:28:54.954
in the history of the city of Boston,

547
00:28:54.989 --> 00:28:56.494
and you need time to think about it?

548
00:28:56.529 --> 00:28:59.395
Before you go flying any
further off the handle,

549
00:28:59.443 --> 00:29:03.504
it might help to recall that
Whitey Bulger is an ex-convict

550
00:29:03.571 --> 00:29:06.813
and that his parole category
is "supervised released status,"

551
00:29:06.848 --> 00:29:09.725
a designation that we would
be required to get withdrawn

552
00:29:09.760 --> 00:29:12.817
or else we would be in
violation of Bureau regulations.

553
00:29:12.852 --> 00:29:15.200
So? We withdraw or we violate.

554
00:29:15.235 --> 00:29:17.904
What we don't do, unless
we're clinically insane,

555
00:29:17.939 --> 00:29:20.054
is blow this chance!

556
00:29:20.856 --> 00:29:23.827
By the way, it's "Jimmy," not "Whitey."

557
00:29:23.862 --> 00:29:24.726
The only thing you're gonna get

558
00:29:24.761 --> 00:29:27.115
by calling him Whitey is a fucking smack.

559
00:29:27.150 --> 00:29:28.518
Oh, is that so?

560
00:29:28.618 --> 00:29:31.028
So I'm supposed to cater
to this fucker's whims?

561
00:29:31.063 --> 00:29:33.441
If it brings you Angiulo, yes!

562
00:29:33.496 --> 00:29:35.737
And what makes you so sure

563
00:29:35.786 --> 00:29:37.283
that he's gonna be a reliable source?

564
00:29:37.318 --> 00:29:38.668
Because in my experience,

565
00:29:38.703 --> 00:29:39.987
everyone of those Winter Hill pricks

566
00:29:40.022 --> 00:29:42.103
is a double-crossing cocksucker.

567
00:29:42.205 --> 00:29:44.311
I grew up with him in Southie.

568
00:29:44.638 --> 00:29:47.902
Jimmy, his brother Billy, and me.

569
00:29:47.949 --> 00:29:51.596
And that is a bond that doesn't get broken.

570
00:29:51.864 --> 00:29:54.777
I mean, if he gives me
his word, he will keep it.

571
00:29:54.831 --> 00:29:57.280
So we're relying on the word of criminals.

572
00:29:57.313 --> 00:29:59.233
Jimmy's no ordinary criminal.

573
00:29:59.283 --> 00:30:01.115
Well, you're right about that.

574
00:30:01.163 --> 00:30:04.618
"A vicious animal who won't
take no for an answer."

575
00:30:04.662 --> 00:30:08.106
"Violent decisiveness
at any hint of betrayal."

576
00:30:08.236 --> 00:30:09.106
Oh!

577
00:30:09.141 --> 00:30:12.511
"A ripened psychopath determined
to succeed above all else."

578
00:30:12.546 --> 00:30:14.369
I got a lot of respect for you, Charles,

579
00:30:14.404 --> 00:30:17.590
but I cannot fucking
believe what I'm hearing.

580
00:30:17.658 --> 00:30:20.490
Four Mafia murders in the
North End this month alone,

581
00:30:20.525 --> 00:30:23.139
and we don't have a
legitimate case on any of them.

582
00:30:23.174 --> 00:30:24.741
The Angiulos are out there laughing at us

583
00:30:24.815 --> 00:30:27.517
like we're fuckin' a bunch of clowns!

584
00:30:27.615 --> 00:30:29.998
A bunch of clowns!

585
00:30:30.065 --> 00:30:30.947
Come on, guys.

586
00:30:31.022 --> 00:30:34.524
If we're serious about
bringing down the Italians,

587
00:30:34.629 --> 00:30:36.286
Jimmy is the only way.

588
00:30:36.319 --> 00:30:38.453
What about these LSD experiments in prison?

589
00:30:38.488 --> 00:30:39.706
He can't be stable.

590
00:30:39.741 --> 00:30:41.483
He did it for time off and money.

591
00:30:41.518 --> 00:30:42.968
And it was a handful of times.

592
00:30:43.029 --> 00:30:45.503
It was 50 times, John.

593
00:30:46.937 --> 00:30:48.786
Just trust me when I tell you

594
00:30:48.821 --> 00:30:53.190
he is a smart, stable motherfucker.

595
00:30:55.536 --> 00:30:57.589
What do you think, Morris?

596
00:31:00.861 --> 00:31:04.783
I think that we have more
to gain than to lose on this.

597
00:31:04.844 --> 00:31:06.746
I think we go with John.

598
00:31:07.062 --> 00:31:11.252
I think we bring Whitey...
uh, Jimmy, into the tent.

599
00:31:18.459 --> 00:31:22.251
No drugs. No fuckin' murder, Connolly.

600
00:31:24.096 --> 00:31:28.144
_

601
00:31:32.224 --> 00:31:33.979
_

602
00:31:36.741 --> 00:31:38.448
_

603
00:31:45.454 --> 00:31:48.893
You listen good, 'cause
I'm only gonna say this once.

604
00:31:49.117 --> 00:31:52.715
I will never hurt or adversely affect

605
00:31:52.750 --> 00:31:55.879
any of my friends or financial partners.

606
00:31:55.978 --> 00:31:59.903
I do not consider this
rattin' or informin'.

607
00:32:00.003 --> 00:32:01.324
This is business.

608
00:32:01.397 --> 00:32:03.384
I couldn't have said it any better.

609
00:32:03.585 --> 00:32:05.364
You're a liaison.

610
00:32:05.498 --> 00:32:07.829
- You pretty much do whatever you want.
- _

611
00:32:07.879 --> 00:32:09.263
And no one's gonna raise an eyebrow

612
00:32:09.298 --> 00:32:12.424
so long as you're leadin' us
into some pretty big busts.

613
00:32:12.459 --> 00:32:13.800
There's just one restriction

614
00:32:13.835 --> 00:32:15.313
- on our side...
- _

615
00:32:16.576 --> 00:32:19.241
you can't kill anybody, Jimmy.

616
00:32:22.973 --> 00:32:25.775
Kevin, did you know
that Whitey was an informant?

617
00:32:25.830 --> 00:32:27.776
No, I didn't know.

618
00:32:27.882 --> 00:32:29.517
I mean, he hated rats.

619
00:32:29.583 --> 00:32:32.843
We fuckin' buried rats, especially our own.

620
00:32:32.991 --> 00:32:35.383
I mean, I knew he had his
connections in the FBI.

621
00:32:35.418 --> 00:32:36.585
I knew he had his sources.

622
00:32:36.645 --> 00:32:38.252
But I figured he was playing them

623
00:32:38.287 --> 00:32:40.155
like he did everybody else.

624
00:32:40.630 --> 00:32:43.366
But obviously, he had a plan.

625
00:32:47.309 --> 00:32:50.311
Where do you get the
energy for that shit, Jimmy?

626
00:32:52.521 --> 00:32:54.962
Hey, Steve. Hang on a minute.

627
00:32:56.879 --> 00:32:59.462
We've known each other a long fuckin' time.

628
00:33:02.823 --> 00:33:04.937
Can I trust you, Stevie?

629
00:33:06.202 --> 00:33:07.873
You know you can trust me.

630
00:33:07.940 --> 00:33:09.455
Good.

631
00:33:10.122 --> 00:33:12.477
'Cause there's something
I want you to know.

632
00:33:14.969 --> 00:33:17.204
I'm making a deal with the Feds.

633
00:33:18.001 --> 00:33:19.770
An alliance.

634
00:33:19.910 --> 00:33:21.799
You're informing to the FBI?

635
00:33:21.834 --> 00:33:25.599
No. There's informing, and
then there's <i>informing.</i>

636
00:33:25.725 --> 00:33:28.429
Informing, you should be fucking chopped up

637
00:33:28.484 --> 00:33:30.731
and put into a garbage bag, that's it.

638
00:33:30.805 --> 00:33:32.662
Informing, you're the scum of the scum.

639
00:33:32.710 --> 00:33:35.438
But it's not informing

640
00:33:35.518 --> 00:33:38.147
when you're bringing down the cocksuckers

641
00:33:38.248 --> 00:33:40.990
who deserve to be brought down...

642
00:33:41.153 --> 00:33:43.635
like the fucking Brits in the six counties

643
00:33:43.700 --> 00:33:47.106
or the goddamn Dagos up in the North End.

644
00:33:47.228 --> 00:33:49.439
It's a business opportunity.

645
00:33:49.474 --> 00:33:53.379
Get the FBI to fight our wars

646
00:33:53.790 --> 00:33:56.472
against our enemies...

647
00:33:57.497 --> 00:33:58.959
while they protect us,

648
00:33:59.020 --> 00:34:01.857
and we do whatever the fuck we want to do.

649
00:34:15.583 --> 00:34:17.423
All right, Jimmy.

650
00:34:20.574 --> 00:34:22.958
There's a guy named John Connolly.

651
00:34:23.166 --> 00:34:25.215
He's a Southie boy. We grew up together.

652
00:34:25.250 --> 00:34:26.374
He's all right.

653
00:34:30.664 --> 00:34:32.578
So, we're doing this?

654
00:34:32.727 --> 00:34:35.097
Yeah, we're gonna do this.

655
00:35:05.314 --> 00:35:06.959
Ho-ho-ho!

656
00:35:07.217 --> 00:35:10.574
Shh, he's asleep. He's a little sick.

657
00:35:11.439 --> 00:35:14.711
He's a little sick? Sick with what?

658
00:35:14.849 --> 00:35:16.709
He's just got a fever.

659
00:35:16.828 --> 00:35:19.770
He'll be fine in a few days.
It's probably just the flu.

660
00:35:19.898 --> 00:35:22.162
Did you take him to the doctor?

661
00:35:22.197 --> 00:35:24.334
No, he'll be okay.

662
00:35:25.508 --> 00:35:28.445
Take him to the doctor
in the morning, would you?

663
00:35:48.928 --> 00:35:50.426
It's only a little,
but it might get bigger

664
00:35:50.461 --> 00:35:52.910
because the hose, at this time of the year,

665
00:35:52.945 --> 00:35:55.079
it's always leaking
and bursting, that pipe.

666
00:35:55.114 --> 00:35:56.943
You want me to get Tom to fix it?

667
00:35:57.030 --> 00:35:59.575
Sure. It's nice of you, Billy, thank you.

668
00:35:59.608 --> 00:36:02.544
No worries. No worries.

669
00:36:02.599 --> 00:36:05.868
Marianne, how are you
settling into Southie?

670
00:36:05.949 --> 00:36:07.081
How do you find it?

671
00:36:07.116 --> 00:36:08.116
I like it.

672
00:36:08.163 --> 00:36:09.628
It's taking a little getting used to,

673
00:36:09.663 --> 00:36:12.416
but... it's different.

674
00:36:12.789 --> 00:36:14.591
Different how?

675
00:36:15.222 --> 00:36:17.227
I find it a rather tight-knit community.

676
00:36:17.262 --> 00:36:20.344
And I could have hoped to have
met a few more people by now.

677
00:36:20.471 --> 00:36:22.880
You know, those sort of
things just take a little time

678
00:36:22.915 --> 00:36:25.475
and you need introductions to people.

679
00:36:25.544 --> 00:36:27.067
Mary and I can help with
that. Can't we, Mary?

680
00:36:27.115 --> 00:36:28.600
Yeah, indeed we can, Bill.

681
00:36:28.671 --> 00:36:30.368
- That would be great, thank you.
- Once you settle in,

682
00:36:30.403 --> 00:36:32.807
you'll find that people around
here are as good as gold.

683
00:36:32.842 --> 00:36:34.031
I'm sure that's true.

684
00:36:34.066 --> 00:36:35.619
Well, of course.

685
00:36:39.781 --> 00:36:43.712
♪ <i>Dashing through the snow
in a one-horse open sleigh</i> ♪

686
00:36:43.780 --> 00:36:46.105
♪ <i>O'er the fields we go,
laughing all the way</i> ♪

687
00:36:46.187 --> 00:36:51.142
All right, everybody. On
the count of 3... 1, 2, 3.

688
00:36:51.373 --> 00:36:53.975
Merry Christmas, everybody!

689
00:36:54.010 --> 00:36:56.498
Boys, come back down here
in five minutes, you hear?

690
00:36:56.564 --> 00:36:57.564
Can we open presents?

691
00:36:57.598 --> 00:36:59.602
Open presents, right.

692
00:37:00.346 --> 00:37:02.619
Whose turn is it first?

693
00:37:03.444 --> 00:37:04.513
That was you?

694
00:37:04.606 --> 00:37:06.026
I don't know how

695
00:37:06.061 --> 00:37:07.843
your brother does it.

696
00:37:07.878 --> 00:37:08.622
What's that?

697
00:37:08.657 --> 00:37:10.559
Nine children.

698
00:37:11.015 --> 00:37:11.807
Oh.

699
00:37:11.938 --> 00:37:15.538
That's a complete mystery to me, as well.

700
00:37:15.691 --> 00:37:16.737
Hello?

701
00:37:18.007 --> 00:37:20.680
Hey, Stevie. I just wanted to say...

702
00:37:20.715 --> 00:37:22.178
I can't understand... calm down.

703
00:37:22.213 --> 00:37:25.875
It's really good that you're comin' along.

704
00:37:25.946 --> 00:37:29.032
It makes things in my world a lot easier.

705
00:37:29.064 --> 00:37:29.905
All right, all right.

706
00:37:29.940 --> 00:37:32.392
- Sure, John.
- Hold on, hold on.

707
00:37:33.795 --> 00:37:35.618
Jimmy, phone.

708
00:37:36.156 --> 00:37:37.379
What?

709
00:37:37.585 --> 00:37:39.688
You need to take the call.

710
00:37:48.556 --> 00:37:51.669
Excuse me. Douglas Cyr's room, please.

711
00:37:51.915 --> 00:37:53.514
Room 508, around the corner.

712
00:37:53.549 --> 00:37:55.164
Thank you.

713
00:37:56.535 --> 00:37:57.860
How is he?

714
00:37:57.924 --> 00:37:59.828
He's in there right now with the doctor,

715
00:37:59.863 --> 00:38:01.785
and they're saying that
it's Reye's syndrome.

716
00:38:01.820 --> 00:38:03.359
What the fuck is Reye's syndrome?

717
00:38:03.394 --> 00:38:05.089
- I thought it was the flu.
- I know, so did I.

718
00:38:05.124 --> 00:38:07.001
But then when you left,
I called the doctor,

719
00:38:07.036 --> 00:38:08.992
and they said to just
keep giving him aspirin

720
00:38:09.040 --> 00:38:11.498
every four hours, just like
I'd been doing for days.

721
00:38:11.533 --> 00:38:12.871
But then his fever got higher,

722
00:38:12.906 --> 00:38:16.717
and then... and then his
behavior started changing,

723
00:38:16.752 --> 00:38:19.013
and he became really angry to me.

724
00:38:19.048 --> 00:38:20.347
Okay.

725
00:38:20.382 --> 00:38:23.940
Like, really angry, and
his body was all stiff,

726
00:38:23.975 --> 00:38:25.266
so I brought him here, and they said

727
00:38:25.301 --> 00:38:29.893
that the aspirin that I had been
giving him just made him worse.

728
00:38:30.180 --> 00:38:32.156
- No. No.
- Yeah, that's what they said!

729
00:38:32.191 --> 00:38:35.140
That's what they said...
that I made him worse.

730
00:38:52.515 --> 00:38:54.826
Sorry, no change.

731
00:39:02.821 --> 00:39:04.880
I'm taking him home, Lindsey.

732
00:39:05.362 --> 00:39:07.411
I don't fucking care what they say.

733
00:39:07.446 --> 00:39:09.634
I want to take my boy home.

734
00:39:09.700 --> 00:39:11.586
He's not coming home, Jimmy.

735
00:39:11.621 --> 00:39:15.956
Don't say that, please. Don't say that.

736
00:39:21.925 --> 00:39:24.882
He's on life support, Jimmy.
He's not going anywhere.

737
00:39:24.969 --> 00:39:26.743
You got to accept it.

738
00:39:26.891 --> 00:39:30.025
I don't got to do fucking nothing.

739
00:39:31.891 --> 00:39:33.259
Look at me.

740
00:39:36.193 --> 00:39:37.910
Jimmy, please look at me.

741
00:39:41.238 --> 00:39:44.920
He's never gonna be our
little boy again, never.

742
00:39:44.999 --> 00:39:46.015
Don't.

743
00:39:46.050 --> 00:39:47.450
- He's brain-dead.
- Don't say that.

744
00:39:47.482 --> 00:39:50.365
He's on life support, he can't move,

745
00:39:50.400 --> 00:39:52.625
and I don't want him like that!

746
00:39:53.048 --> 00:39:55.634
I can't have my little boy be like that!

747
00:40:03.952 --> 00:40:05.988
I'll pull the plug myself.

748
00:40:06.194 --> 00:40:07.813
I will.

749
00:40:12.848 --> 00:40:14.449
What did you say?

750
00:40:23.209 --> 00:40:26.012
What the fuck did you just say?

751
00:40:28.055 --> 00:40:29.924
My boy?

752
00:40:31.439 --> 00:40:34.597
You pull the plug on my boy?

753
00:40:34.848 --> 00:40:37.685
I can't have him like this, Jimmy.

754
00:40:40.847 --> 00:40:43.044
- How could you be so cold?
- Don't say that to me.

755
00:40:43.079 --> 00:40:45.506
- How could you be so cold?
- Don't say that.

756
00:40:45.563 --> 00:40:46.606
I could never, ever.

757
00:40:46.641 --> 00:40:48.920
- Don't you dare fucking say that.
- You're pathetic.

758
00:40:48.955 --> 00:40:50.884
You of all people in
the whole fucking world

759
00:40:50.932 --> 00:40:54.118
- cannot say that to me!
- Who the fuck are you?

760
00:40:54.672 --> 00:40:56.921
You motherfucker.

761
00:40:57.590 --> 00:40:59.894
Go fuck yourself.

762
00:42:01.044 --> 00:42:02.665
Because you have been convicted

763
00:42:02.727 --> 00:42:05.528
of federal racketeering and murder charges

764
00:42:05.563 --> 00:42:08.796
and aim to make a deal to spare your life,

765
00:42:08.864 --> 00:42:11.884
I'd like to start with the
period of Mr. Bulger's life

766
00:42:11.951 --> 00:42:13.641
after the death of his son,

767
00:42:13.676 --> 00:42:14.976
when his enterprise expanded

768
00:42:15.044 --> 00:42:19.705
and he became a so-called
"crime lord" of Boston.

769
00:42:24.451 --> 00:42:26.071
Okay.

770
00:42:36.552 --> 00:42:40.034
From what were you and Mr.
Bulger making your money?

771
00:42:40.590 --> 00:42:42.297
Ah, it was a lot of things...

772
00:42:42.332 --> 00:42:44.412
running dope on the streets of Southie.

773
00:42:44.445 --> 00:42:47.823
We had the rackets. We had the ponies.

774
00:42:48.017 --> 00:42:49.487
Tenants on every corner.

775
00:42:49.556 --> 00:42:51.056
This ain't your neighborhood, Whitey.

776
00:42:51.091 --> 00:42:52.493
Is that right?

777
00:42:52.638 --> 00:42:55.482
But we were
making weekly collections.

778
00:42:55.557 --> 00:42:56.817
Fuck you, fuck you, fuck you!

779
00:42:56.932 --> 00:42:59.850
You name it, and yeah, we was doin' it.

780
00:43:00.297 --> 00:43:01.645
The lottery, Jimmy?

781
00:43:01.680 --> 00:43:03.693
- _
