a little sit-down here.

1538
01:22:18.627 --> 01:22:22.970
What the fuck did you
marinate this steak in?

1539
01:22:23.033 --> 01:22:24.631
Because it's out of this world.

1540
01:22:24.666 --> 01:22:26.167
You're killing me with it.

1541
01:22:26.202 --> 01:22:28.238
Now, now, now.

1542
01:22:28.584 --> 01:22:31.104
It's a family secret. Hmm?

1543
01:22:31.402 --> 01:22:33.863
Come on.

1544
01:22:33.964 --> 01:22:35.268
Aw.

1545
01:22:35.399 --> 01:22:37.390
That is one of the best goddamn steaks

1546
01:22:37.425 --> 01:22:39.528
- I ever had in my life.
- Mm-hmm.

1547
01:22:39.605 --> 01:22:40.840
Ever.

1548
01:22:44.644 --> 01:22:47.213
I got a knife over here.

1549
01:22:47.297 --> 01:22:49.035
Oh, come on. Come on.

1550
01:22:49.098 --> 01:22:50.753
What's... what's the...
what's the family...

1551
01:22:50.813 --> 01:22:52.574
what's the family's secret recipe?

1552
01:22:52.609 --> 01:22:54.884
It's g... it's ground garlic

1553
01:22:54.936 --> 01:22:57.460
and a little bit of soy.

1554
01:22:57.508 --> 01:23:00.479
- That's it?
- Yeah, that's it. That's it.

1555
01:23:08.179 --> 01:23:10.983
I thought it was a family secret.

1556
01:23:13.914 --> 01:23:16.257
It's a recipe.

1557
01:23:16.311 --> 01:23:17.862
No.

1558
01:23:19.017 --> 01:23:20.465
No.

1559
01:23:21.320 --> 01:23:24.075
You said to me this is a family secret,

1560
01:23:24.110 --> 01:23:27.081
and you gave it up to me, boom.

1561
01:23:27.185 --> 01:23:30.622
Just fucking like that.

1562
01:23:31.236 --> 01:23:32.203
Don't look to John

1563
01:23:32.251 --> 01:23:34.635
'cause he's not gonna fucking help you.

1564
01:23:39.899 --> 01:23:43.403
You spill the secret family recipe today,

1565
01:23:43.438 --> 01:23:45.913
maybe you fucking spill about me tomorrow.

1566
01:23:45.948 --> 01:23:48.772
Is that something, maybe,
that's a possibility?

1567
01:23:48.807 --> 01:23:49.781
I was just saying...

1568
01:23:49.816 --> 01:23:51.652
You were "just saying"?

1569
01:23:51.778 --> 01:23:55.615
"Just saying" gets
people sent to Allenwood.

1570
01:23:55.681 --> 01:23:59.187
"Just saying" got me a nine-year stretch

1571
01:23:59.222 --> 01:24:01.175
in Leavenworth and Alcatraz.

1572
01:24:01.210 --> 01:24:02.687
You understand?

1573
01:24:02.722 --> 01:24:06.442
So, "just saying"...

1574
01:24:07.626 --> 01:24:11.464
could get you buried real fucking quick.

1575
01:24:29.327 --> 01:24:31.516
Look at his fucking face!

1576
01:24:31.551 --> 01:24:34.321
Hey! I'm fucking with you.

1577
01:24:34.354 --> 01:24:35.686
Hey, I'm fucking with you.

1578
01:24:35.721 --> 01:24:37.922
It's a recipe. Couldn't give a shit.

1579
01:24:37.973 --> 01:24:40.861
Tastes great. I'm fucking with you.

1580
01:24:41.602 --> 01:24:43.115
All right.

1581
01:24:43.150 --> 01:24:46.119
You got... well, you... you got me, too.

1582
01:24:47.033 --> 01:24:49.700
Listen, I... I want to...
I want to make a toast.

1583
01:24:51.050 --> 01:24:52.719
To success.

1584
01:24:54.198 --> 01:24:56.434
Just getting started.

1585
01:25:03.427 --> 01:25:06.793
Mm. Where's the wife?

1586
01:25:07.027 --> 01:25:08.781
She's, uh... she's resting.

1587
01:25:08.816 --> 01:25:11.152
She's... she's a little under the weather.

1588
01:25:12.883 --> 01:25:15.686
Didn't... didn't I just see her?

1589
01:25:15.917 --> 01:25:17.163
Yeah, she was helping.

1590
01:25:17.228 --> 01:25:20.715
She, uh... well, sh... sh...
she's not feeling very good.

1591
01:25:20.869 --> 01:25:22.156
Oh, gee.

1592
01:25:22.230 --> 01:25:23.589
Like a...

1593
01:25:23.716 --> 01:25:25.967
You know what? I'll go have a look at her.

1594
01:25:26.074 --> 01:25:27.282
Jimmy. Jimmy.

1595
01:25:27.317 --> 01:25:28.800
She's sick. She's fi... she's fi...

1596
01:25:28.835 --> 01:25:30.400
listen... fine.

1597
01:25:51.463 --> 01:25:52.174
Oh.

1598
01:25:52.209 --> 01:25:54.613
Hi. I thought you were John.

1599
01:25:55.275 --> 01:25:57.742
No, it ain't John.

1600
01:25:57.803 --> 01:26:00.952
Come on. Come down and join us.

1601
01:26:00.998 --> 01:26:03.444
No, I'm not feeling
well. Thank you, though.

1602
01:26:04.179 --> 01:26:05.714
Marianne, you know what you're doing?

1603
01:26:05.749 --> 01:26:08.449
You're embarrassing your
husband in front of his friends,

1604
01:26:08.497 --> 01:26:09.833
that's what you're doing.

1605
01:26:09.914 --> 01:26:12.584
And you know that's what you're doing.

1606
01:26:13.048 --> 01:26:16.200
I don't know what John told
you, but I'm feeling ill.

1607
01:26:18.020 --> 01:26:19.559
That's all.

1608
01:26:19.726 --> 01:26:21.686
Please, no offense.

1609
01:26:24.461 --> 01:26:26.906
Well, let's see what you got.

1610
01:26:27.358 --> 01:26:29.184
Um...

1611
01:26:30.458 --> 01:26:32.135
yeah.

1612
01:26:35.039 --> 01:26:37.068
Well...

1613
01:26:37.827 --> 01:26:40.558
you don't feel warm.

1614
01:26:42.259 --> 01:26:44.325
Got any chills?

1615
01:26:45.249 --> 01:26:46.797
'Cause normally, you get the chills

1616
01:26:46.832 --> 01:26:49.430
before the flu comes on, you know?

1617
01:26:53.151 --> 01:26:55.254
Any soreness there?

1618
01:26:57.428 --> 01:27:01.358
What are you feeling
there? You feel something?

1619
01:27:03.181 --> 01:27:06.910
'Cause I don't feel any
swollen glands there.

1620
01:27:08.560 --> 01:27:14.755
But, you know, me, I
had to learn the hard way

1621
01:27:15.781 --> 01:27:18.710
not to take chances
with this kind of thing.

1622
01:27:18.771 --> 01:27:21.040
You know what I'm saying?

1623
01:27:22.726 --> 01:27:24.772
Poor little thing.

1624
01:27:25.851 --> 01:27:27.860
You get some rest.

1625
01:27:28.020 --> 01:27:30.345
Wouldn't want nothing to happen to you.

1626
01:27:40.432 --> 01:27:42.867
John's a lucky man.

1627
01:28:14.577 --> 01:28:15.858
Jimmy?

1628
01:28:17.305 --> 01:28:19.599
I'll get it there safe and sound.

1629
01:28:19.946 --> 01:28:21.777
You can sleep on it.

1630
01:28:21.887 --> 01:28:23.847
I know you will, McIntyre.

1631
01:28:23.919 --> 01:28:25.851
Have safe travels, huh?

1632
01:28:26.407 --> 01:28:28.116
All right.

1633
01:28:28.151 --> 01:28:28.826
Stevie.

1634
01:28:28.861 --> 01:28:30.818
Take care of it, John.

1635
01:28:31.364 --> 01:28:33.248
Weeksy, give me a call.

1636
01:28:33.368 --> 01:28:35.686
Thanks for everything,
Jimmy. We won't forget it.

1637
01:28:35.721 --> 01:28:37.199
For me, it's an honor.

1638
01:28:37.287 --> 01:28:38.888
The honor's ours.

1639
01:28:39.198 --> 01:28:40.636
Thanks, pal.

1640
01:28:52.492 --> 01:28:55.514
_

1641
01:28:57.344 --> 01:28:59.252
Hope I'm not interrupting.

1642
01:28:59.284 --> 01:29:01.138
Special Agent John Connolly.

1643
01:29:01.173 --> 01:29:02.806
I know who you are. I've
heard a lot about you.

1644
01:29:02.841 --> 01:29:04.862
Oh, good things, I hope.

1645
01:29:04.957 --> 01:29:07.495
Listen, little welcome
wagon present for you.

1646
01:29:07.589 --> 01:29:09.525
- Big game.
- I'm good.

1647
01:29:09.560 --> 01:29:11.898
Are you sure about that?
Clemens is on the mound tonight.

1648
01:29:11.933 --> 01:29:13.478
I'm sure about that.

1649
01:29:13.513 --> 01:29:15.016
All right.

1650
01:29:15.133 --> 01:29:16.697
Work, work, work.

1651
01:29:16.778 --> 01:29:18.714
Well, listen, after... after you finish,

1652
01:29:18.749 --> 01:29:20.736
come down to
The Bell-In-Hand.

1653
01:29:20.806 --> 01:29:22.670
I would like to buy you a pint,

1654
01:29:22.705 --> 01:29:25.212
and you can meet some of the other agents.

1655
01:29:27.263 --> 01:29:30.077
Do you have a case for me, Agent Connolly?

1656
01:29:30.112 --> 01:29:32.851
No, I just came to i... introduce myself.

1657
01:29:32.886 --> 01:29:35.332
You know, couple of local
boys moving up the ranks.

1658
01:29:35.387 --> 01:29:38.465
Maybe we can help each other along. Yeah.

1659
01:29:38.527 --> 01:29:41.489
Bring me cases, that's all the help I need.

1660
01:29:42.260 --> 01:29:43.641
All right.

1661
01:29:45.289 --> 01:29:48.141
All right, well,
I'll leave you to it, then.

1662
01:29:48.278 --> 01:29:49.707
Hey, you know, since you're here.

1663
01:29:49.742 --> 01:29:51.014
Yeah?

1664
01:29:51.429 --> 01:29:53.481
How come no one has nailed Whitey Bulger?

1665
01:29:53.516 --> 01:29:55.445
Oh, no. No, no, no.

1666
01:29:55.480 --> 01:29:57.863
That won't work. I wouldn't
do that if I were you.

1667
01:29:57.898 --> 01:30:00.079
- Excuse me?
- Now, what's Bulger done?

1668
01:30:00.148 --> 01:30:05.061
He's a smalltime hood, but he...
he... he's an invaluable asset.

1669
01:30:05.243 --> 01:30:07.658
What's he done?

1670
01:30:07.726 --> 01:30:10.000
Everything, evidently.

1671
01:30:10.035 --> 01:30:13.048
Drugs, extortion, murder.

1672
01:30:13.163 --> 01:30:13.906
I'd heard rumors,

1673
01:30:13.961 --> 01:30:16.234
but these other informant
reports make it clear.

1674
01:30:16.269 --> 01:30:17.055
And he... here's the thing...

1675
01:30:17.090 --> 01:30:20.053
every time we start a
formal investigation, poof!

1676
01:30:20.193 --> 01:30:22.408
Goes away. He slips free.

1677
01:30:22.668 --> 01:30:24.709
How do you account for that?

1678
01:30:24.833 --> 01:30:26.125
I don't know.

1679
01:30:26.760 --> 01:30:29.425
Luck of the Irish?

1680
01:30:29.545 --> 01:30:31.420
"Luck of the Irish"? That's
what you're going with?

1681
01:30:31.455 --> 01:30:33.524
Well, it's...

1682
01:30:35.165 --> 01:30:37.587
...it's slandering lies

1683
01:30:37.622 --> 01:30:40.025
from his brother Billy's
political opponents.

1684
01:30:40.060 --> 01:30:42.071
These fucking assholes from Cambridge,

1685
01:30:42.106 --> 01:30:43.949
they will do anything to bring Billy down

1686
01:30:43.984 --> 01:30:45.586
because they can't stand

1687
01:30:45.621 --> 01:30:48.054
power in the hands of a Mick from Southie.

1688
01:30:48.089 --> 01:30:49.112
You don't think Billy's protecting

1689
01:30:49.147 --> 01:30:50.566
his older brother, just maybe?

1690
01:30:50.601 --> 01:30:52.243
No! No way.

1691
01:30:52.326 --> 01:30:53.833
Really?

1692
01:30:54.164 --> 01:30:54.964
Well, it seems to me

1693
01:30:54.999 --> 01:30:56.512
you'd have to believe
in fucking leprechauns

1694
01:30:56.580 --> 01:30:59.658
to think we have the
biggest crime lord in Boston

1695
01:30:59.804 --> 01:31:02.241
and be brothers with the
most powerful politician

1696
01:31:02.276 --> 01:31:05.942
in the state and them <i>not</i>
be helping each other out.

1697
01:31:05.977 --> 01:31:09.085
I grew up with Billy, Southie.

1698
01:31:09.163 --> 01:31:12.124
So, I know him, I know that <i>he</i> knows

1699
01:31:12.159 --> 01:31:13.079
that it would be crazy

1700
01:31:13.114 --> 01:31:15.950
for him to get mixed up in
anything that Jimmy does.

1701
01:31:16.027 --> 01:31:18.978
It's, you know... too brazen.

1702
01:31:19.091 --> 01:31:20.860
I'll ask you again...

1703
01:31:20.900 --> 01:31:23.662
how come no one has done Whitey Bulger?

1704
01:31:23.758 --> 01:31:26.431
He seems to be involved
in every crime in the city

1705
01:31:26.466 --> 01:31:28.606
and yet the Bureau keeps saying he's clean.

1706
01:31:28.654 --> 01:31:30.987
It's only when <i>another</i>
agency has an informant

1707
01:31:31.022 --> 01:31:33.840
that I hear <i>maybe</i>
Whitey isn't so squeaky clean.

1708
01:31:36.074 --> 01:31:37.449
Well, I hear that he's very careful,

1709
01:31:37.484 --> 01:31:41.488
he doesn't use phones...
that kind of stuff, and, uh...

1710
01:31:41.967 --> 01:31:45.043
Who did you say these
other informants were?

1711
01:31:45.459 --> 01:31:47.091
I didn't.

1712
01:31:49.564 --> 01:31:51.744
Listen, from what I hear,

1713
01:31:51.857 --> 01:31:53.741
his criminal days are all but over.

1714
01:31:53.776 --> 01:31:56.152
His... his partner and
him, they gone legit...

1715
01:31:56.187 --> 01:31:58.327
Christ, Connolly, you fucking with me?!

1716
01:31:58.362 --> 01:32:00.395
Is Whitey never using phones and careful,

1717
01:32:00.430 --> 01:32:02.209
or is Whitey retired?!

1718
01:32:02.256 --> 01:32:03.624
I don't...

1719
01:32:04.709 --> 01:32:06.807
I mean, I just... I'm not in my office...

1720
01:32:06.842 --> 01:32:08.111
these are things that I hear,

1721
01:32:08.146 --> 01:32:09.583
I don't know if all of them are true.

1722
01:32:09.618 --> 01:32:12.125
Do your job and find out!

1723
01:32:15.240 --> 01:32:17.809
I am. I am. I... I wa...

1724
01:32:18.766 --> 01:32:22.276
You know that I wouldn't come
here if it wasn't serious,

1725
01:32:22.427 --> 01:32:23.875
if there was anywhere else I could turn,

1726
01:32:23.910 --> 01:32:25.880
and I know that the last thing you need

1727
01:32:25.915 --> 01:32:29.079
is to have Jimmy's business
crossing paths with yours.

1728
01:32:29.114 --> 01:32:31.042
Well, your grasp of the
situation is so keen,

1729
01:32:31.077 --> 01:32:32.743
it makes me wonder what you're doing here.

1730
01:32:32.778 --> 01:32:37.392
This new guy, Wyshak, has
a serious hard-on for Jimmy.

1731
01:32:37.427 --> 01:32:39.239
And that can't be good for any of us.

1732
01:32:39.302 --> 01:32:40.706
And you're telling me this why?

1733
01:32:40.772 --> 01:32:42.827
Maybe you can influence him.

1734
01:32:42.862 --> 01:32:44.030
Just make him listen to reason!

1735
01:32:44.065 --> 01:32:45.851
I'm not kissing your ass, Billy,

1736
01:32:45.892 --> 01:32:48.364
but you are the most
powerful man in the city.

1737
01:32:48.399 --> 01:32:50.136
Not that I would, but Wyshak's federal,

1738
01:32:50.184 --> 01:32:51.784
and I'm state, and you know that.

1739
01:32:51.819 --> 01:32:56.289
But where we come from, I know and you know

1740
01:32:56.324 --> 01:32:59.922
that what is written on a piece of paper

1741
01:33:00.054 --> 01:33:06.137
is less important than
blood and honor and loyalty.

1742
01:33:09.839 --> 01:33:12.195
I'm not asking you to help me.

1743
01:33:12.950 --> 01:33:15.453
I'm asking you to help your brother.

1744
01:33:17.888 --> 01:33:20.463
That's the same thing now, isn't it?

1745
01:33:31.922 --> 01:33:39.353
Billy, Wyshak is asking
questions about you, too.

1746
01:33:42.085 --> 01:33:43.647
Oh.

1747
01:33:50.289 --> 01:33:53.447
John, you know I have the
utmost respect for you.

1748
01:33:53.482 --> 01:33:57.446
Really, I do, which is why I
can tell you with all my heart

1749
01:33:57.617 --> 01:33:59.696
that if you ever come into my office again

1750
01:33:59.751 --> 01:34:01.664
with a fucked-up idea like that

1751
01:34:01.699 --> 01:34:05.406
you'll rue the day you ever
thought of joining the FBI.

1752
01:34:10.789 --> 01:34:12.659
Jeannie will show you out.

1753
01:34:21.594 --> 01:34:22.842
This report has information

1754
01:34:22.877 --> 01:34:26.989
attributed to our prized
informant Whitey Bulger.

1755
01:34:30.131 --> 01:34:32.416
And this is the same piece of information

1756
01:34:32.451 --> 01:34:34.587
from one of our other informants

1757
01:34:34.679 --> 01:34:36.281
dated four weeks earlier.

1758
01:34:36.315 --> 01:34:40.201
_

1759
01:34:40.236 --> 01:34:41.783
This is information credited to

1760
01:34:41.818 --> 01:34:45.912
our supposedly prized
informant James "Whitey" Bulger.

1761
01:34:49.068 --> 01:34:51.584
- And the same piece of information
- _

1762
01:34:51.619 --> 01:34:55.913
dated six weeks earlier,
different informant.

1763
01:34:56.265 --> 01:34:57.674
_

1764
01:34:57.709 --> 01:34:59.695
In fact, if you take a
look at Bulger's pile,

1765
01:34:59.760 --> 01:35:01.400
you'll find the same situation played out

1766
01:35:01.430 --> 01:35:03.387
time and again from other sources.

1767
01:35:03.462 --> 01:35:09.978
In fact, you'll find very little
from Bulger that means shit.

1768
01:35:15.867 --> 01:35:18.829
<i>Customs officials in Boston
say they have seized a trawler</i>

1769
01:35:18.883 --> 01:35:21.819
<i>used to smuggle weapons
to Irish terrorists.</i>

1770
01:35:21.854 --> 01:35:24.625
<i>Agents say the trawler ferried
a load of arms and ammunition</i>

1771
01:35:24.660 --> 01:35:26.859
- <i>to the Irish coast last week.</i>
- Jesus fucking Christ.

1772
01:35:26.894 --> 01:35:29.440
<i>The weapons were intercepted
by the Irish Navy</i>

1773
01:35:29.475 --> 01:35:32.031
<i>after they had been
transferred to a smaller ship.</i>

1774
01:35:32.082 --> 01:35:35.242
- <i>Officials say they have seized the ship's log and other doc...</i>
- Motherfucker.

1775
01:35:35.267 --> 01:35:37.035
Northern Ireland?

1776
01:35:37.115 --> 01:35:38.350
Yeah.

1777
01:35:40.697 --> 01:35:42.472
Well, how did they know about the ship?

1778
01:35:42.507 --> 01:35:45.265
The pilot. Turns out he's
also a snitch for D.E.A.

1779
01:35:45.332 --> 01:35:46.925
Customs, too.

1780
01:35:48.299 --> 01:35:50.021
What's his name?

1781
01:35:50.231 --> 01:35:51.882
- I don't know.
- How do you not know?

1782
01:35:51.917 --> 01:35:54.979
I... don't know, John.

1783
01:35:58.007 --> 01:36:01.544
All right, well, where is
this guy now, the pilot?

1784
01:36:01.640 --> 01:36:04.243
- I want to talk to him.
- Oh, no can do.

1785
01:36:04.306 --> 01:36:06.712
What do you mean, "No can do"? Yes, can do.

1786
01:36:06.763 --> 01:36:08.527
Sorry, he belongs to D.E.A.

